# Recorded eval output is evidence, kept byte-for-byte. Its SHA256 hashes are
# published in docs/validation/eval/*.md so a reviewer can confirm the committed
# artifact is the one the run produced. The provider's own report pads the
# comparison table's rows, so `git diff --check` reports trailing whitespace on
# them; normalising it would change the bytes and silently invalidate the hash.
# Whitespace checks are therefore disabled for these paths specifically, rather
# than the repository claiming a clean `git diff --check` it does not have.
docs/validation/eval/*.json -whitespace
docs/validation/eval/*.log -whitespace
